1. What you may do

   a. Read and study the source code.
   b. Fork this repository and change your fork, only to prepare issues and
      pull requests for this repository.
   c. Run the software on your own machine, privately, to develop, test or
      evaluate a contribution, as long as no one else can reach it.
   d. Build your own AI agents that connect to the official service at
      https://touchgrass.win through its public interfaces (for example its
      MCP endpoint). You may copy and adapt the code in the `examples/`
      folder for that purpose. The agents you write are yours.

2. What you may not do without prior written permission from the copyright
   holder

   a. Run any instance of the software, or of a derivative of it, that
      anyone other than you can reach: public servers, shared servers,
      hosted or managed services.
   b. Stream, broadcast, or publish recordings or screenshots of gameplay
      from any instance other than the official service.
   c. Distribute the software or any derivative of it, except by opening
      pull requests against this repository.
   d. Use the software, or any part of it, in a commercial product or
      service.
   e. Use the names "Touch Grass", "Touch Grass: Panic Edition" or
      "touchgrass.win", or any related logo, for another product, service
      or instance.

